    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;760;-1808,-656;Inherit;False;350.074;161.9404;;;0,0,0,1;The
    Ward approach to Anisotropic BRDF produces drastically different results than
    the Trowbridge-Reitz method. $$The Specular highlight is much softer, and dissapates
    much faster as the surface proceeds in smoothness $$;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;789;-4464,-1072;Inherit;False;290.4297;157.1641;Anisotropic;;0,0,0,1;Use
    the float to set the direction of the anisotropy effect. Negative values make
    the effect vertical, and positive values make the effect horizontal.  This stretches
